1|0@pics^1438841421#cttauyz:blackoutdaddy$:Bases do have storage options, the problem is they suck. It was TMO when I was in. You would park your car in the "rot lot" where if you were lucky you could prep your car for long term storage, but make sure you write down your mileage because some fuckstick may take your mustang for a ride. Same shithead is rooting through your stored personal property at the warehouse. Even when things go well, it takes them a month or more to get things out of storage. The first time I got back from Iraq, locals in 29 Palms had gotten civilian clothing ready for us, so we could leave the base and have some Liberty. (Marines are not allowed to wear combat uniforms off base). Anywho, you have options. Best one is, throw your shit in a pile, set it on fire, because at least it is cathartic and somewhat fun. TV off the third deck is also a good one. I am not bitter.
